id: pm-34xisz
title: Package-declared internal commands leak into default runtime contracts
description: "An isolated package registering an arbitrary command with tier internal and family internal is omitted from public help but remains in default contracts --flags-only. collectExtensionCommandContracts drops registration tier metadata and default filtering consults only core command identities. Preserve dynamic package tier metadata through SDK contract assembly, command/action discovery and explicit full/scoped inspection."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:contracts","area:sdk",extensions,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-09-12T08:56:50.560Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T09:22:46.527Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: An arbitrary installed package internal command is absent from default command and action discovery; full and explicit scoped contracts retain the command and its declared tier; standard package commands remain discoverable; real temporary-package tests cover both visibility classes
parent: pm-n7rr
expected_result: Package authors control internal discovery through their declared SDK tier without adding names to the core table
actual_result: Temporary package internal-probe secret-worker appears in default and full contracts commands and command_flags while public help hides it
